# The checks of the team's own project (own_project in bin/lib/team.sh) that no merge waits on:
# their findings show on a PR and are fixed in a task of their own, and neither a red nor a pending
# one holds a PR, a merge or the merge queue. A committed constant, never a registry key, since
# the registry is a record any session can edit.
# One line each: the workflow's file name under .github/workflows/, one space, the check's name
# (its job's). team-ci-wait neither waits on such a check or its workflow's run nor fails on it,
# and pr_part (team-state, team-merge, team-catch-up) keeps it out of the passed, failing and
# pending checks. A name the project's required_checks or the base's rules require is never passed
# over, and no other project's check of the same name is. Each workflow runs on pull requests and
# by hand, never on a merge queue's trial commit, and no job of it is a required check, which
# tests/repo.bats holds.
rust-macos.yml rust-macos
